\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When all Thy mercies, O my God,
\par My rising soul surveys,
\par Transported with the view, I'm lost
\par In wonder, love and praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Unnumbered comforts on my soul
\par Thy tender care bestowed,
\par Before my infant heart conceived
\par From whom those comforts flowed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Though hidden dangers, toils, and deaths,
\par It gently cleared my way;
\par And through the passing snares of vice,
\par More to be feared than they.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Ten thousand thousand precious gifts
\par My daily thanks employ;
\par Nor is the least a thankful heart,
\par That takes those gifts with joy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Through every period of my life
\par Thy goodness I'll pursue;
\par And after death, in distant worlds,
\par The glorious theme renew.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Through all eternity, to Thee
\par A grateful song I'll raise;
\par But O eternity's too short
\par To utter all Thy praise!
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

